    "name": "Authentication - EIS OAuth Token",
    "description": "This API retrieves OAuth tokens through client credential flow for use in authenticating to EIS APIs.\n\n## Service Domain Role:\n\nRetrieve OAuth token for use in Authorization HTTP header when calling EIS APIs.  \nCustomer/party authentication is a cross-channel/device capability that provides identity confirmation for customers accessing the bank through any interactive channel. The service may use a combination of one or more mechanisms to authenticate including issued tokens/devices, virtual mechanisms such as passwords and biometrics such as voice/face recognition. Different levels of authentication may be determined to support different types of access and there may be access permissions associated with the authentication mechanism used.\n\n## Example of Use:\n\nA customer is authenticated when making phone contact with the bank's service center.  \nProviding a client ID and client secret, this API will return an OAuth token that can be used in the authorization header when calling EIS APIs.\n\n## Detailed Summary:\n\nCapture and process authentication requests Access issued device details to perform authentication Support multiple device/additional tasks to raise authentication Return access permissions associated with issued authentication devices.  \nBy providing a client ID and client secret, this API will return an OAuth token that can be used in the authorization header when calling EIS APIs. This API is intended to be used by service integrations with the EIS platform.\n\nContact Support:  \nName: EIS  \nEmail: [EISSupportTeam@seacoastbank.com](https://mailto:EISSupportTeam@seacoastbank.com)",
